title: Heath Speaks Out
tags: event
view-if: heath_hostility >= 70 and random_roll < 0.2 and time - last_heath_outburst >= 4
max-visits: 3
new-page: true
on-arrival: last_heath_outburst = time; wet_dissent += 5; thatcher_rating -= 2

= Heath Speaks Out

Edward Heath has given another interview criticising the direction of the party. He doesn't mention you by name; he never does.

- @rebuke: Have the party chairman rebuke him.
- @ignore: Rise above it.
- @olive_branch: Send Willie Whitelaw to see him.

@rebuke
on-arrival: heath_hostility += 5; dry_dissent -= 3; wet_dissent += 2

Lord Thorneycroft issues a sharp statement. The dries are delighted, and the feud runs for another week.

@ignore
on-arrival: wet_dissent += 1

You say you have nothing to add to Mr Heath's remarks. The story dies, slowly.

@olive_branch
on-arrival: heath_hostility -= 10; wet_dissent -= 3; dry_dissent += 2

Whitelaw spends an evening at Heath's flat in Wilton Street. It doesn't end the feud, but it cools it.
